  <sysml:NestedConnectorEnd xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1512986905164_791768_226619" xmi:uuid="f326d370-fa39-013a-046d-52540000fd3c">
    <propertyPath xmi:idref="_18_4_1_271a0567_1512986755134_438620_226074"/>
    <base_ConnectorEnd xmi:idref="_18_4_1_271a0567_1512986905158_857045_226615"/>
  </sysml:NestedConnectorEnd>
  <uml:Package xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499433278411_811722_28110" xmi:uuid="5d5a2585-b0ed-437e-bc2a-956600872116" xmi:type="uml:Package">
    <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8e001ed_1510149613689_682537_31080" xmi:uuid="6f8e71eb-a02a-49a9-a289-e5351bb3da3c" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
      <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499433278411_811722_28110"/>
      <body>This capability represents information to associate parts with shape and with the role of this shape. A shape description may consist of several portions that may be related and their roles. The figure below provides an overview of the capability. &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;ShapeAssociation_domainModel_overview.png&lt;/name&gt;Simplified overview of the AP242 shape association and structure Domain model&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;br&gt; Key entities and associated relationships:&lt;br&gt; A ShapeElement identifies a piece of the shape of either: &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;an AssemblyViewRelationship,&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;a BreakdownElementView,&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;an IndividualPartView,&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;an Occurrence (see subtype OccurrenceShapeElement),&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;a PartView (see subtype PartShapeElement),&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;a ProductConfiguration,&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;a ShapeFeatureDefinition (see subtype ShapeFeatureDefinitionElement),&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;or another ShapeElement.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; A ShapeElement can be represented by a DetailedGeometricModelItem.&lt;br&gt; The attribute ProductDefinitional specifies if the ShapeElement identifies a piece of the boundary of the target object.&lt;br&gt; Two ShapeElements can be related with each other by a ShapeElementRelationship.&lt;br&gt; Two or more ShapeElements can be joined or constrained with each other by AssemblyShapeJoint or AssemblyShapeConstraint respectively (see Mating capability).&lt;br&gt; ShapeFeatureDefinition is the identification of a part of some shape independently of a target element, so that it can be used multiple times as &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_ShapeAssociationAndStructure.htm#PartShapeElement.Definition&lt;/path&gt; Definition&lt;/a&gt; for ShapeElements such as PartShapeElements. ShapeFeatureDefinitionElement identifies a piece of a ShapeFeatureDefinition and ShapeFeatureDefinitionElementRelationship relates two of them. ShapeFeatureDefinitionRelationship relates two ShapeFeatureDefinitions and the subtype ShapeFeatureDefinitionFitRelationship characterizes that these two ShapeFeatureDefinitions fit together. &lt;br&gt; With the attribute &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_ShapeAssociationAndStructure.htm#ShapeFeatureDefinitionElementRelationship.ParentRelationship&lt;/path&gt; ParentRelationship&lt;/a&gt; of ShapeFeatureDefinitionElementRelationship, it is possible to set-up a hierarchical structure of two ShapeFeatureDefinitions with elements. ShapeFeatureDefinitionOccurrenceElement represents an element in a higher level ShapeFeatureDefinition that is defined by lower level ShapeFeatureDefinition or ShapeFeatureDefinitionElement. A ShapeFeatureDefinitionOccurrenceElementRelationship is used to state which ShapeFeatureDefinitionOccurrenceElements corresponds to each other. &lt;br&gt;</body>
    </ownedComment>
    <name>ShapeAssociationAndStructure</name>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1513614520064_305173_47496" xmi:uuid="003b56c2-445a-4fbd-983e-cab7c197f159" xmi:type="uml:Association">
