    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193242_442446_23839" xmi:uuid="6eaf7008-a346-4e0a-92da-8143f19462f0" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456415325988_819419_43128" xmi:uuid="4fa3cf67-885c-4666-bc73-703ebe0485ed" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193242_442446_23839"/>
        <body>A ShapeElement is a portion of shape that has to be identified explicitly to be associated with other information. &lt;note&gt; A ShapeElement may be a CoatingLayer. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; ShapeElement objects can be classified using Class. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt; In order to identify a portion of one face of a shaft that shall have a surface coating applied to it, ShapeElement is used. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;example&gt; An example for classifying ShapeElement objects is to identify all parts of an air plane that constitute the outer surface of the plane and are therefore relevant for aerodynamic analyses. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;example&gt; The threaded portion of the shape of a bolt may be represented as a ShapeElement, so that other properties, such as surface finish, may be associated with it.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551200412635_929074_128777" xmi:uuid="ad4180ae-67d1-441d-b661-6e1728382b9d" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_290014c_1550847743191_208266_98071"/>
        <body>These flowports are not bound to the ARM target because only a product definition property type can be assigned to it.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>ShapeElement</name>
